@startuml feature_v4_F-003_sequence
' Runtime truth for F-003 v4 — Platform invariant gates
' The cast below is the `participants:` list of feature_v4_F-003_front-matter.yaml, name for name.
' One group per story; one group per failure mode the front matter declares.
title F-003 v4 — Platform invariant gates
autonumber

actor "Contributor" as Contributor
participant "pre-commit" as PreCommit
participant "GitHub Actions" as Actions
participant "Repository validators" as Validators
participant "Terraform preconditions" as Preconditions
database "Checkov baseline" as Baseline
database "Toolchain versions" as ToolVersions
database "Workflow files" as Workflows
database "Cluster registry" as Registry

group F-003-US1 — an accepted supply-chain finding carries a reason, an owner and an expiry
  Contributor -> PreCommit : git commit touching the checkov baseline
  PreCommit -> Validators : python3 scripts/validate-checkov-baseline.py
  Validators -> Baseline : read the _schema header and every checkov_baseline_finding
  Baseline --> Validators : suppression entries
  Validators --> PreCommit : exit 0
  PreCommit --> Contributor : the commit is allowed
end

group F-003-US2 — exactly one file declares a toolchain version
  PreCommit -> Validators : python3 scripts/validate-tool-version-singleton.py
  Validators -> ToolVersions : read every tool_version_pin
  Validators -> Workflows : scan the workflows and Dockerfiles for a second declaration
  Workflows --> Validators : no second declaration
  Validators --> PreCommit : exit 0
end

group F-003-US3 — every workflow action reference is a commit SHA carrying a tag comment
  PreCommit -> Validators : python3 scripts/validate-action-pins.py
  Validators -> Workflows : read every uses: reference
  Workflows --> Validators : every reference is a 40-character SHA with its tag comment
  Validators --> PreCommit : exit 0
end

group F-003-US4 — a malformed cluster catalogue fails before anything consumes it
  PreCommit -> Validators : python3 scripts/validate-cluster-registry.py
  Validators -> Registry : load through the same loader the consumers use
  Registry --> Validators : cluster_entry records
  Validators -> Validators : validate against registry.schema.json and check that each key equals its aks_name
  Validators --> PreCommit : exit 0
  Contributor -> Actions : open a pull request touching terraform
  Actions -> Preconditions : terraform plan
  Preconditions -> Preconditions : evaluate the region_abbrev and spoke-versus-hub CIDR preconditions before any provider work
  Preconditions --> Actions : the plan proceeds
end

group F-003-US5 — no sensitive value reaches a chart through a set-value
  PreCommit -> Validators : python3 scripts/validate-helm-release-secrets.py
  Validators -> Validators : match every set-value against the curated sensitive-attribute list, following one alias hop
  Validators --> PreCommit : exit 0; a Secret named by reference is allowed
end

group F-003-US6 — binary entry points stay wiring-only
  PreCommit -> Validators : bash scripts/validate-mgmt-plane-lock-runners.sh
  Validators -> Validators : check every cmd main.go is at most 40 lines and imports no os/signal
  Validators --> PreCommit : exit 0
end

group F-003-US7 — the pull request carries a readable plan
  Actions -> Validators : python3 scripts/truncate-plan-output.py
  Validators --> Actions : output at or under the threshold passes through unchanged; oversize output is truncated with a footer
  Actions --> Contributor : the plan comment on the pull request
end

== Failure modes ==

group failure — a suppression is missing its metadata
  Validators -> Baseline : read each checkov_baseline_finding
  Baseline --> Validators : an entry without a rationale, an owner or an expiry
  Validators --> Contributor : non-zero exit naming the entry index and the missing field
end

group failure — a toolchain version is declared twice
  Validators -> Workflows : scan for a version declaration outside the pin file
  Workflows --> Validators : a second declaration
  Validators --> Contributor : non-zero exit naming the offending file
end

group failure — an action is referenced by tag rather than by commit SHA
  Validators -> Workflows : read the uses: references
  Workflows --> Validators : a reference that is not a 40-character SHA
  Validators --> Contributor : a file-and-line annotation and a non-zero exit
end

group failure — a cluster catalogue entry does not match the schema
  Validators -> Registry : validate against registry.schema.json
  Registry --> Validators : an entry with a missing or malformed field
  Validators --> Contributor : non-zero exit naming the entry
end

group failure — a catalogue key and its aks_name disagree
  Validators -> Registry : load through the shared loader
  Registry --> Validators : the loader raises before any consumer sees the entry
  Validators --> Contributor : non-zero exit naming the key and the name
end

group failure — a region short code is not in the canonical map
  Actions -> Preconditions : terraform plan
  Preconditions --> Actions : the precondition fails and the plan aborts with the formatted message
end

group failure — a spoke network range equals a hub range
  Actions -> Preconditions : terraform plan
  Preconditions --> Actions : the precondition fails and the plan aborts before any provider work
end

group failure — a sensitive value is passed to a chart as a set-value
  Validators -> Validators : the set-value matches the curated sensitive-attribute list
  Validators --> Contributor : non-zero exit naming the release and the attribute
end

group failure — a binary entry point handles signals itself
  Validators -> Validators : a cmd main.go exceeds 40 lines or imports os/signal
  Validators --> Contributor : non-zero exit naming the binary
end

group failure — a platform-managed secret has no expiry
  Validators -> Validators : python3 scripts/validate-akv-null-expiry.py reads NULL_EXPIRY_MODE
  Validators --> Contributor : advisory mode prints the finding and exits 0; blocking mode exits non-zero
end

note over Validators, Preconditions
  invariants: DOM-003-R1, DOM-003-R2, DOM-003-R3, DOM-003-R4, DOM-003-R5,
  DOM-003-R6, DOM-003-R7, DOM-003-R8, DOM-003-R9, DOM-003-R10
  timeout: none — every validator is a local synchronous process over the committed tree
  retry: none — a gate is deterministic over its input, so re-running changes nothing
  idempotency: total — the gates read and never write
  degraded: none, by design. A gate blocks; it does not fall back.
  The only variable behaviour is the expiry check, whose advisory-or-blocking
  mode comes from NULL_EXPIRY_MODE and is not visible from the script.
end note

@enduml
